course: dictionary
lesson: 2646
title: Detention and other school words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, so check the sentence to see which one fits. «Maddie got a detention for the shove» tells you a detention is a punishment, because she was given it for doing something wrong. At school, a detention means staying in after lessons or at break time.
explain: Context clues help you work out the meaning. «A detention or lost play time is a consequence» shows that a detention is one kind of consequence, which means something that happens because of what you did. Ask yourself: would the sentence still make sense if I put my meaning in place of the word?
explain: The word can also mean being kept somewhere by police or other officials so you cannot leave. The sentences in this lesson are about school, so the school meaning fits. Always check which meaning the text is using.
fact: A detention is a punishment at school where a pupil must stay in after lessons or at break time.
fact: «Get a detention» means you are given one, and «be in detention» means you are serving it now.
fact: «After-school detention» and «lunchtime detention» tell you when the detention happens.
fact: Detention can also mean being kept somewhere by police or other officials so you cannot leave.
fact: A consequence is what happens because of what you did, and a detention is one kind of consequence.
exercise: «Connor was excluded for two days, and Maddie got a detention for the shove.» What is a detention? | *A punishment where a pupil must stay in after lessons or at break time | A type of school lunch | A prize for good work | A fun club to join after school
exercise: «Jake got a detention and a letter home.» Which phrase in this sentence tells you the detention was given to him? | letter home | and a letter | Jake got | *got a detention
exercise: «Sam has an after-school detention.» When does Sam have to stay in? | At lunchtime | At the start of the morning | *After the school day ends | On a weekend trip
test: «Maddie got a detention for the shove.» Which meaning of detention fits here? | *A school punishment where she must stay in | A visit to the doctor | A prize for helping the class | Being kept by police so she cannot leave
test: «A detention or lost play time is a consequence.» What is a consequence? | *Something that happens because of what you did | A type of school lesson | A word for a school trip | A friend who helps you
exam: Which phrase tells you a detention happens at break time? | after-school detention | be in detention | *lunchtime detention | get a detention
